// The art book's frame for the entry round (doc/workflows/art_book.md, step 0): written once for the game, composed around each brief's entry. The user's wording of 2026-10-18: the pitch, the figure, and the presentation of a hand painted illustration without a page, since the frame took half the picture and the lettering leaked.
pitch = "A factory builder game on planets, from the surface down into the caves and up to orbit: mining, refining, automation and logistics. Stylised realism: real light on real materials, simplified shapes, low texture detail, no outlines, no cartoon palette. Machines are compact and squat, packed into their box, one big readable feature each, painted panels chipped at the edges to the metal, grime in the seams, moss taking hold where it is cool and damp, lit by what glows."
figure = "a futuristic dark with orange accent EVA suited astronaut"
presentation = "Drawn and painted by hand as a concept illustration: pencil construction lines showing through, visible brush strokes, painterly edges, not a 3D render, not a screenshot. No other machine is showing. No lettering whatsoever. No frame and no game UI."
